{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured `/srv/drop` on node1 as a root-owned shared directory with mode 1777. Live tests before and after reboot proved users can create and remove their own files but cannot remove files owned by other users. The directory persisted through the mandatory reboot and was left empty.","actions_performed":["Created `/srv/drop` with owner `root:root` and mode `1777` (`drwxrwxrwt`).","Tested shared writes and sticky-bit deletion protection using two temporary users.","Restarted node1 safely and confirmed its boot ID changed.","Verified directory metadata, test data, and sticky-directory behavior after restart.","Removed all temporary users, files, and restart evidence data."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Configure `/srv/drop` as shared writable while preventing users from removing files owned by others","command_ids":["cmd-9b2c487d915344a8","cmd-64b08a5ddc2f4d40","cmd-4cff20330c3c40dc"],"summary":"Shows root ownership and mode 1777, successful writes by distinct users, cross-user deletion denied with `Operation not permitted`, owner deletion succeeding, and the final empty directory state."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-2d6e856334dd49a0","cmd-b4fd06c22e784e44","cmd-09898271601d4660","cmd-99dc86b8f94444ec"],"summary":"Captures the healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, reboot acknowledgement, changed post-restart boot ID, persisted marker hash/content, retained mode 1777, and successful post-restart behavioral testing."}]}
